### Portal API — manual/exploratory test suite
#
# These requests exercise the PUBLIC, unauthenticated `/portal/*` endpoints consumed by
# `apps/portal` (see sls/functions/portal.yml). No Cognito token is required.
#
# How to use:
#   VS Code  -> install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client), open this file,
#               pick an environment in the bottom-right status bar ("dev" or "local"),
#               then click "Send Request" above each block.
#   JetBrains (WebStorm/IntelliJ) -> open this file, pick the environment from the
#               dropdown next to the run icon, click the green run arrow per request.
#
# Environments are defined in ./http-client.env.json:
#   - dev   -> https://dev-api.collectshare.com.br (deployed dev stage; API has no local server)
#   - local -> http://localhost:3000 (only if you run `serverless offline` yourself)
#
# Before running the dataset-specific requests, set `formId` in http-client.env.json
# (or override the @formId variable below) to a form with `isPublished: true`.
# You can find one by running the "Search datasets" request first and copying a
# `formId` from the `results` array of the response.

@formId = {{formId}}

### 1. Search datasets — semantic search (proxies Algolia), default relevance sort
GET {{baseUrl}}/portal/search?q=educação
Accept: application/json

### 2. Search datasets — empty query (returns default/browsable listing)
GET {{baseUrl}}/portal/search
Accept: application/json

### 3. Search datasets — sorted by trending (requires ALGOLIA_TRENDING_INDEX_NAME configured)
GET {{baseUrl}}/portal/search?q=saúde&sort=trending
Accept: application/json

### 4. Get published dataset metadata (form + questions)
# Also increments the dataset's click count as a side effect.
GET {{baseUrl}}/portal/datasets/{{formId}}
Accept: application/json

### 5. Get published dataset metadata — unknown/unpublished form (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/portal/datasets/this-form-does-not-exist
Accept: application/json

### 6. Get paginated raw submission data — first page
GET {{baseUrl}}/portal/datasets/{{formId}}/data?limit=5
Accept: application/json

### 7. Get paginated raw submission data — next page
# Copy `nextCursor` from the previous response's body into the `cursor` param below.
GET {{baseUrl}}/portal/datasets/{{formId}}/data?limit=5&cursor=PASTE_NEXT_CURSOR_HERE
Accept: application/json

### 8. Get paginated raw submission data — limit clamped to MAX_LIMIT (100) when exceeded
GET {{baseUrl}}/portal/datasets/{{formId}}/data?limit=500
Accept: application/json

### 9. Export dataset as CSV
# Also increments the dataset's download count as a side effect.
# Response is `text/csv` with a Content-Disposition attachment header, not JSON.
GET {{baseUrl}}/portal/datasets/{{formId}}/export
Accept: text/csv
